#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0462 expect=violation domain=EC
#note "ECDOSTXT column absent while row 1 has ECDOSE empty, ECOCCUR=Y (!=N) and ECSTAT empty. Requirements.Variables.All [ECDOSTXT] now gates the rule out -> auditable skip naming the column instead of a violation carried by the bare empty(ECDOSTXT) leaf (absent = all-missing, EC-43). Verdict 2-1 (T1-32): the absence is itself reportable, and the minted sister CDISC-CG9673 reports it ONCE for this dataset."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset EC label="Exposure as Collected"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ECSEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col ECOCCUR type=Char label="Occurrence"
col ECSTAT type=Char label="Completion Status"
col ECDOSE type=Num label="Dose per Administration"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | EC | 01-701-1015 | 1 | Y |  |
CDISCPILOT01 | EC | 01-701-1023 | 2 | Y |  | 100
